  "id": "COMPOUND:22242 - PROTEIN:6000",
  "verbalization": "Commersonine is implicated in the regulation of Lysosomal phospholipase A2 through a series of molecular interactions involving the DNMT3A2/3L complex. This complex is targeted by multiple compounds, including (R)-(-)-2-Amino-1-propanol, Juzirine, and Suksdorfin, all of which share a common pathway of targeting the DNMT3A2/3L complex and ultimately leading to the inhibition of Lysosomal phospholipase A2. The evidence suggests that Commersonine may exert its effects through a similar mechanism, possibly by modulating the DNMT3A2/3L complex, which in turn influences the activity of Lysosomal phospholipase A2. The consistent involvement of the DNMT3A2/3L complex as a target in multiple pathways underscores a potential shared regulatory role, although the exact mechanism by which Commersonine interacts with this complex remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these findings highlights a possible link between Commersonine and Lysosomal phospholipase A2 through a pathway involving the DNMT3A2/3L complex, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
